Do not treat "[" as a bracket expression in y.
The y command shares the delimiter scan of s, which skips over a
bracket expression in the regex so that a delimiter inside it does not
end the regex. But the source string of y is a plain list of
characters, not a regex, so a "[" in it hid the delimiters that
followed: "y/[/x/" and "y/[a/]x/" failed with "unmatched '/'" instead
of mapping "[" to "x", and "[" and "a" to "]" and "x". Scan the source
of y without bracket expressions, as is already done for the
replacement of s and the destination of y, which matches GNU sed.

